# Merge, rebase, and patch leftovers. This project integrates many parallel
# branches, and a committed `*.orig` is the most common way that scratch reaches
# a reader.
*.orig
*.rej
*.patch.tmp

# Local agent and assistant configuration (machine-specific, not project state)
.claude/
.aider*

# Repository-local caches and scratch directories
/$cache/
/tmp/
*backup*.jsonl

# Session scratch at the repository root. Four such scripts were committed by
# accident and carried one author's worktree layout, five private branch
# worktree names, the evidence store path and a local image digest into the
# handover. The rule is anchored to the root on purpose: `_*` unanchored would
# swallow every package `__init__.py`.
/_*

# Development handover notes. A tracked NEXT_SESSION.md published a private
# branch name, a worktree path, an open-bug backlog and the owner's TODOs.
# Session state belongs in the issue tracker, never in the published tree.
/NEXT_SESSION.md
/HANDOFF.md
/HANDOVER.md
/SESSION_*.md
/NOTES.md
/TODO.md

# Rendered figures and console captures. They are produced from the console for
# external write-ups, not shipped with the tool, and they would otherwise carry
# case-specific values into the repository.
docs/tui/
docs/figures/

# Evaluation and CTF measurement harness, not part of the shipped tool.
/tools/examiner_ask.sh
/deploy/console/ctf.sh
